# Saloon Girl/Barmaid

**Alignments.** Any, but often selfish or evil.

The Saloon Girl works the floor of a saloon, a dance hall or a gambling house -
singing, dancing, serving, and above all talking to people who have had a few
drinks and want to be listened to. That last part is the trade: she hears a
great deal, and what she hears has value.

She may sell it to anyone who will pay, the Coalition included. Some are petty
thieves who roll drunks. Some take a little bounty hunting, smuggling or
assassination on the side. The book is enthusiastic about the range of the
character and recommends her as a non-player character first - especially the
two-timing cheats, informers, spies, thieves and assassins.

## Lore

Also known as the Barmaid, the Gold-digger, the Tease and the Seductress.

She is the natural partner of the Professional Gambler, who often works with a
sidekick to signal opponents'' hands, and of the Sheriff, whom the book names her
and the Saloon Bum as likely informers for.
', 'published', 'data-script'
WHERE NOT EXISTS (SELECT 1 FROM imported_classes WHERE class_id = 'saloon-girl');


